          %p
            there is a unique function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h\colon Y \to X
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi A
                  %mi h
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi q
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_A h = q_A
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi B
                  %mi h
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi q
                    %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_B h = q_B\,.
          %p
            Since this universal property expresses the concept of pullback purely arrow-theoretically, we can formulate it in any category. It is, in fact, a simple special case of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#in_category_theory In category theory
          %h4#as_a_limit As a limit
          %p
            A
            %strong pullback
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            like this:
