            %p
              of the two morphisms induced by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              out of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
          %p
            As a consequence of the above, any category with binary products and equalizers has pullbacks. Conversely any category with binary products and pullbacks has equalizers: the equalizer of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g:A \to B
            is the pullback of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} maps
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,f) \maps A \to A \times B
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} maps
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,g) \maps A \to A \times B
          #PullbackPreservesMonomorphisms.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (pullbacks preserve monomorphisms and isomorphisms)
            %p
              Pullbacks preserve
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
              and
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
            %p If
