            %p
              Then the left square and the outer rectangle are pullbacks but the right square cannot be a pullback unless
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              was already an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              On the other hand, in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
              = succeed "." do
                %em homotopy pullback – homotopy fiber characterizationullback#HomotopyFiberCharacterization)
          %h3#saturation Saturation
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/saturated+class+of+limits"} saturation
            of the class of pullbacks is the class of limits over categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            whose groupoid reflection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1(C)
            is trivial and such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-finite+category"} L-finite
          %h3#PullbackFunctor Pullback functor
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X \to Y
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            with pullbacks, there is an induced pullback
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*\colon C/Y \to C/X
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
          %div
            %p
              %strong Notions of pullback:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"}> pullback
                  ,
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+product"} fiber product
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
                  over a
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cospan"} cospan
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wide+pullback"} wide pullback
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+pullback"}> weak pullback
                  ,
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-pullback"} quasi-pullback
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+pullback"}> lax pullback
                  ,
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+object"} comma object
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+limit"} lax limit
                  over a cospan)
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"}> (∞,1)-pullback
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limit"} (∞,1)-limit
                  over a cospan)
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"}> base change
                  ,
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context+extension"} context extension
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+bundle"} pullback bundle
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contravariant+functor"} contravariant functor
                %ul
                  %li
                    %p
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+in+cohomology"}> pullback in cohomology
                      ,
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/d-invariant"} d-invariant
                  %li
                    %p
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+of+differential+forms"} pullback of differential forms
                  %li
                    %p
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+of+a+distribution"} pullback of a distribution
          %h2#references References
          %p Early use of the terminology “pullback”:
          %ul
            %li#Mitchell65
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barry+Mitchell"}> Barry Mitchell
              , Section I.7 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Theory of categories
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 17
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.elsevier.com/books/theory-of-categories/mitchell/978-0-12-499250-4"} ISBN:978-0-12-499250-4
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li#MacLane
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+MacLane"}> Saunders MacLane
                , p. 71 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+for+the+Working+Mathematician"} Categories for the Working Mathematician
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4757-4721-8"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4757-4721-8
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
                , Section 2.5 in Vol. 1:
                %em Basic Category Theory
                of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Categorical+Algebra"} Handbook of Categorical Algebra
                %strong 50
                Cambridge University Press (1994) (
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511525858"}> doi:10.1017/CBO9780511525858
                )
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joyal"}> André Joyal
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/joyalscatlab/published/Cartesian+squares"} Cartesian squares
          %p
            In view of more general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-finite+limits"} L-finite limits
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completion"} completion
            of a category under pullbacks:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Par%C3%A9"}> Robert Paré
              ,
              = succeed "." do
                %em Simply connected limits
              %a{:href => "http://math.ca/10.4153/CJM-1990-038-6"} CMS
          %p
            Morphisms admitting pullbacks along them are called
            %strong carrable
            in some places, for instance, the following:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+Toen"}> Bertrand Toen
              ,
              %em A master course on algebraic stacks (Toulouse 2005)
              cours 2 (
              %a{:href => "https://perso.math.univ-toulouse.fr/btoen/files/2015/02/cours2.pdf"}> web
              )
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Notes on Clans and Tribes
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1710.10238"} arxiv:1710.10238
          %p
            They are called
            %strong quarrable
            in:
          %ul
            %li#Cockett93
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robin+Cockett"}> Robin Cockett
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Introduction to distributive categories
              %strong 3
              (2009) 277-307 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0960129500000232"}> doi:10.101/S0960129500000232
              \&amp;rbrack;
